                <pb facs="0308" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860d.01/47: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-06T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                                1919, 3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>6247. Please ascertain the views of the Foreign Office with regard to full
                    recognition of Government of Finland.</p>
                <p>It is considered desirable that if full recognition be accorded, it be determined
                    upon contemporaneously by the four principal associated governments.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Paris and Rome.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
